<title>HUNGARY: Hungary twelve-month bill yield falls to 22.72 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary twelve-month bill yield falls to 22.72 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of twelve-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 22.72 percent, down from 22.86 percent at an auction two weeks ago, the Government Debt Management Centre(AKK) said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     14,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	29,046.67 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    14,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 15,500 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    22.72 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     81.6105 pct</p>
</text>
